		{
			title: "Lighting the Way"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "hexagon"
			subtitle: "A New Objective"
			description: [
				"&dOkay, the Glitched Resources are working well. "
				""
				"&5Looks like yer about to hit level 10, Bandit. That should open up a new Objective in the Vaults."
				""
				"&dAnd possibly another way for us to siphon some items out of their servers."
				""
				"&5Oh, its no longer Activate the Monoliths? Light the Braziers..."
				""
				"&dLooks like its a similar idea : There is a Brazier in every room. You need to activate a set amount before exiting the Vault in time."
				""
				"&5This is different though, sis. Looks like each Brazier gives you a good and a bad perk. Sometimes just one..."
				""
				"&dLosing Vault Time, ew. But once you have the set number of Braziers, you can activate more to Pillage them for possible rare loot. Exactly what I was looking for. Go Pillaging, Bandit!"
			]
			dependencies: ["7C074ABF2EDF12C1"]
			id: "76B7D44E338DC9B7"
			tasks: [{
				id: "574C8D2FDC6C0563"
				type: "observation"
				title: "Find a Brazier"
				icon: "woldsvaults:monolith"
				timer: 0L
				observe_type: 0
				to_observe: "the_vault:monolith"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Pillaged and Plundered"
			x: 0.25d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "More System Cracks"
			description: [
				"&dExcellent Bandit, another Completion Crate. And inside should be..."
				""
				"&5...what is that, sis?"
				""
				"&dDear bro, the next step of the plan. Each time you open up a Completion Crate, you get a token like that. They are a symbolic 'link' from inside the FOP Game Server data centers."
				""
				"&5Wait...computer 'link' or magic 'link'?"
				""
				"&dYes."
				""
				"&5Ye know, I should have expected that. Okay, so should Bandit hide the token?"
				""
				"&dNo no, I just needed to get them out of the data center to create the link. Actually, how about we incentivise Bandit getting more of these."
				""
				"&5Token shop?"
				""
				"&dToken shop. Check the Shop Catalogue, Bandit, there's a new section with special rewards you can trade in for."
			]
			dependencies: ["76B7D44E338DC9B7"]
			id: "10F607F18CE03D39"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2B4B2F0651EEFC4C"
				type: "item"
				title: "A Brazier Completion Crate"
				item: "the_vault:vault_crate_monolith"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "324481C298B2397F"
				type: "choice"
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Bare Bones Vaulting"
			x: 2.25d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "Raw Resources (And A Bit More)"
			description: [
				"&dLooking into it Bandit, some Power Users were able to start in what is called a \"Skyvault\" server, a special server in which they start in a void world and have to build their base out."
				""
				"&5...hey, did Bandit start in one? Can we even tell?"
				""
				"&dWe can tell, but it doesn't really change our approach to getting them out, as we'll need a few things from this 'Skyvault' template anyways."
				""
				"&5Oh? Do tell, sis."
				""
				"&dNow, starting with just a tiny island and no resources doesn't really get the FOP anything, right? Except a stuck and bored Power User. So, they created a special type of vault called a Raw Vault."
				""
				"&5Oh! The Raw Vaults, that's right. They contain a lot of the non-Vault resources you need to build a base and gear and machines. Like Iron, Diamonds, Stone, etc."
				""
				"&dRight, and Raw Vaults come from Budding Crystals, which grow like Amethyst. Budding Crystals are usually reserved for Skyvault users, but a tiny little code change and...you can make one, Bandit."
			]
			dependencies: ["10F607F18CE03D39"]
			id: "3E2831A2D27654C0"
			tasks: [{
				id: "29A99E23734A15F1"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:crystal_budding"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "001A41EB98B1D2AA"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Recycling and Reusing"
			x: -6.25d
			y: -3.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Repurposed"
			description: [
				"&dBandit, you'll quickly notice that you'll start getting more and more Vault Gear, and most of it won't be useful to you... as it is now."
				""
				"&5You can still get some use out of the gear, and not just by selling it to us or back to the FOP. You can RECYCLE it!"
				""
				"&dThe Vault Recycler can take Vault Gear, Jewels, and some other vault items and break them down into some resources."
				""
				"&5These resources can usually be used to improve or craft gear in the Vault Forge."
				""
				"&dThe Recycler is also the only way you can get some resources, like Vault Scrap."
			]
			dependencies: ["7543E03FC25521E7"]
			id: "29198B5EA727A867"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6D8D9704EC9248AF"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:vault_recycler"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Pocket Souls"
			icon: {
				id: "the_vault:shard_pouch"
				Count: 1b
				tag: {
					Inventory: { }
				}
			}
			x: -4.0d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Soulful"
			description: [
				"&dYou've probably been through a Vault or two already, Bandit, and you've already gotten quite a few Soul Shards, yes?"
				""
				"&5Even though they stack up to the max, the better you are at fighting the Vault's monsters, the more inventory they'll fill up."
				""
				"&dSeems to encourage Players to fight as much and efficiently as possible, the FOP has included a useful item : the Shard Pouch."
				""
				"&5As long as this Shard Pouch is in your main inventory (not stuck in a backpack), it should collect all the Soul Shards you get."
				""
				"&dSeems a few recipes still need Soul Shards, so you'll need to grab them out yourself. But things like The Black Market can pull out Shards for you."
			]
			dependencies: ["0AF2E388B45934CC"]
			id: "287AFB08CA4CC848"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3091F35A6756D661"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:shard_pouch"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Raw Tap"
			x: 4.25d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "diamond"
			subtitle: "One Token, Two Token, Three Token, Go!"
			description: [
				"&dOkay Bandit, you'll want to run a Raw Vault or two as there's a few things in there you'll want to find."
				""
				"&5Raw Vaults have their own kind of chests. Instead of Wooden, Ornate, etc; they have Hardened and Flesh Chests."
				""
				"&dAnd don't forget the real treasure: Enigma Chests."
				""
				"&5These stand out against the dull gray and browns of the Raw Vaults. They are Obsidian and Purple. And contain special treasure."
				""
				"&dUseful stuff, BUT not required right now, thankfully! They are pretty rare. No, Bandit, right now you just want to open a bunch of Hardened and Flesh Chests to find some Raw Vault Tokens."
				""
				"&5Getting my sister these \"Links\" in as many routes as possible makes our job easier. Like throwing more grapples on an enemy ship, makes em less likely to break free."
			]
			dependencies: ["3E2831A2D27654C0"]
			id: "3011291910FDA2DC"
			tasks: [{
				id: "154F2F7EF5DBE99B"
				type: "item"
