				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Couple Sippies"
			x: -8.25d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Only Approved Drinks Allowed"
			description: [
				"&dSo you probably haven't tried it yet, Bandit, but we wouldn't suggest taking in normal potions like Potions of Healing or the like."
				""
				"&5The FOP didn't like players stacking bags full of potions to stay alive, as that was less resources they'd receive later."
				""
				"&dTheir 'approved' method is to make Vault Vials, Potions, or Brews. These have limited uses, but can regain them one of three ways : "
				""
				"&5Pacifist recharges over time. Slaughterer recharges when you kill enough enemies. And Goblin recharges when you loot enough chests."
				""
				"&dThey also fully recharge between Vault runs, thankfully. For now, you can only make Vials, but with the proper Research you can make bigger, better ones."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["50D9EFE8ABEA9779"]
			id: "600061B7D508477A"
			tasks: [{
				id: "356CD721DA1624B4"
				type: "item"
				title: "Any Vial"
				item: "the_vault:bottle"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Shining Knowledge"
			x: 2.25d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "At a Price"
			description: [
				"&dIn the FOPGame Server, knowledge is power and is not free, unfortunately."
				""
				"&5It's mostly used as a way to encourange Users to gather resources, craft things, and send them to the FOP, of course."
				""
				"&dKnowledge is needed to Research \"mods\" to unlock and use. These mods range from small, singular purpose mods; to big, wide ranging ones."
				""
				"&5\"Mods\" in this case are the different 'product lines' the FOP has stolen for their game server."
				""
				"&dThey get Users to craft these products and submit them for money..."
				""
				"&5...or more Vault crystals..."
				""
				"&dTo get more Knowledge to begin the cycle again. You don't NEED to Research mods, Bandit, but it limits how fast you can make new Vaults, as the cost scales up with each crystal."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["10F607F18CE03D39"]
			id: "50203F008ADF0804"
			tasks: [{
				id: "78917DC8115FDEE1"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:knowledge_star"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "4447A6DCDFC1330B"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "An Affinity For Loot"
			icon: "the_vault:pogging_jewel"
			x: -8.25d
			y: 1.0d
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Breaking, Slicing, and Dicing"
			description: [
				"&dOne thing to note, Bandit, is that Vault Tools are able to break Vault Chests. But only if they have the Affinity for it."
				""
				"&5Aye, ye'll want to make and apply the Affinity for every chest on your Vault Tool, as it greatly speeds up yer looting."
				""
				"&dThough an important thing : Wood Chests and all other chests 'break' differently. Wooden Chests have to be broken as a whole, and take time."
				""
				"&5Aye, and Living, Ornate, and Gilded are 'sliced'. Each slice tosses out one stack of items. But ye can just hold the button down and 'slice n dice' quickly."
				""
				"&dMakes quite a satisfying sound, I have to say."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["3E4FCFC9637F8B61"]
			size: 0.75d
			id: "6E76FC7B7537B0B8"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5BF11E8BDDDF8015"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Shape Indecisions"
			x: -8.25d
			y: 2.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "A Style All It's Own"
			description: [
				"&dThe shape of your Vault Tool depends on which Tool abilities it has. If its just got Picking on it, its a Pickaxe."
				""
				"&5But that changes when ye got Picking and Shoveling. Or Axing and Reaping. Or more of them."
				""
				"&dYeah, but a cool thing happens if you remove ALL the tool abilities. No Picking, no Axing, etc. "
				""
				"&5The system doesn't know what ta show, so it cycles through ALL of them!"
				""
				"&dWe thought this was a cool idea, so we came up with the Stylish Focus and snuck it into the FOPGame System."
				""
				"&5Combine this with yer Vault Tool using an Anvil, and ye keep all the Tool abilities it had, but it ALSO cycles through all the visual styles!"
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["3E4FCFC9637F8B61"]
			id: "43A15992C3676506"
			tasks: [{
				id: "09831D85BA92EB29"
				type: "item"
				item: "woldsvaults:stylish_focus"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Forging a Legacy"
			x: -6.25d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Scrappy to Legendary"
			description: [
				"&dThe Vault Forge is both handy and quite a hog to get the most out of it."
				""
				"&5From it, ye can craft any of the types Vault Gear, at yer level or below."
				""
				"&dBut to start, you'll be very unproficient at it. To increase your skill, you'll need Vault Scrap, which you can get from throwing unused Gear into the Vault Recycler."
				""
				"&5Then take yer Vault Scrap to the Vault Forge, and put em in the slot in the upper right with the same Scrap shape. It takes more and more scrap per level to keep yer proficiency up."
				""
				"&dBut at the same time, you're ability to loot more and faster should increase too, yeah?"
			]
			dependencies: ["7543E03FC25521E7"]
			id: "075AD2D046BFE367"
			tasks: [{
				id: "39B3958325926455"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:vault_forge"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "4D26ECA45A4C5059"
				type: "choice"
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "An Ancient Collection"
			x: 4.25d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Is Posting It Worth More or Less?"
			description: [
				"&dSo the FOP implemented an... interesting system called Antiques. It's...stamp collecting?"
				""
				"&5Aye, a weird choice, but ye can find some crazy valuable stamps out there. How're these found? Just looted?"
				""
				"&dSort of. Looks like each stamp has a specific drop condition. A tiny chance from a specific mob in a specific theme. Or from certain actions."
				""
				"&5Interesting! Looks like there's an Antique Stamp Collector Book ye can make to hold all ye find."
				""
				"&dWhen you collect enough of a certain stamp, you can get a reward."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["3011291910FDA2DC"]
			id: "5D9B2844DF7AD95C"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7EE674F8A8EDF519"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:antique_collector_book"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "0553F9C6B10F8BC2"
				type: "choice"
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Spot for Animals"
			x: -9.75d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Jarred Up"
			description: [
				"&dBandit, the FOPGame Servers have implemented a special early game tool for players to lower system lag."
				""
				"&5They are called Animal Pens, and are good to use early before more options open up."
				""
				"&dYou'll need to start with some Animal Jars. You can Sneak + Right Click them onto most common animals (Cows, Pigs, Sheep, etc) to \"Jar\" them."
				""
				"&5This is a one way process, unfortunately. Ye can't get em back out."
				""
				"&dYou'll need two of an animal to be useful, Bandit. You can then take an Animal Jar with some animals in it, and Right Click it onto a placed Animal Pen."
				""
				"&5Then ye can Right Click the same food ye need to get animals to Breed to...well, do the same thing, just in the pen. Animals like Sheep can be Sheared, same with Bees for Honeycomb."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["69C663CDD23190A9"]
			id: "175A7FF1C22107B1"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "42CE2CFC109F51D7"
					type: "item"
					item: "the_vault:animal_pen"
				}
				{
					id: "00E54450C956F2B2"
					type: "item"
					item: "the_vault:animal_jar"
				}
			]
		}
		{
			title: "Cute Doll"
			x: 4.25d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "It's Staring At Me"
			description: [
				"&dBandit, if you have some Assistants with you, but they aren't always able to run Vaults with you, you might want to look into Vault Dolls."
				""
				"&5Aye, it's a holdover from a previous game the FOP had. They retooled it for Vault Hunters. Ye can have an Assistant make a Vault Doll, and it'll bear their name and character skin. "
				""
				"&dEquip the doll on your head Curios slot. Make sure you aren't in a Vault Party with the Assistant. Then run the Vault. It'll randomly 'copy' some of the loot you collect and store it in itself."
				""
				"&5After the Vault, give the doll back to the Assistant. They can Right Click the Doll onto the ground to release it. CAREFUL, do this in an enclosed area!"
				""
				"&dSee, when you 'release' the doll, it starts to run around. To get your loot, you gotta kill it."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["69C663CDD23190A9"]
			id: "6A5D150DBF70C1E7"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4D9DD070D8342ECD"
				type: "item"
				item: {
					id: "the_vault:vault_doll"
					Count: 1b
					tag: { }
				}
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Box of Mystery"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "What Do You Hold?"
			description: [
				"&dA semi uncommon bit of loot to find, Bandit, is the Mystery Box."
				""
				"&5These can contain a few useful resources. Well...less so than before. It looks like they nerfed the heck out of these..."
				""
				"&dExcuse me? Nope. Can't have that. Let me fix that...."
				""
				"&5Dunno why they changed it. You didn't get tons of these anyways."
				""
				"&dThere. Okay, now you have a small chance of getting rarer Vault Gems from these."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["69C663CDD23190A9"]
			id: "589513669CDDE01C"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1527D2FB9D7D99D5"
